DexSwapModule_OracleSlippage
├── given oracle is fully configured — feed failures
│   ├── when sell token feed returns negative price
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when buy token feed returns negative price
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when sell token feed returns zero price
│   │   └── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when sell token feed is stale
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when buy token feed is stale
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when sell token feed reverts
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when buy token feed reverts
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   └── when decimals() reverts on a feed
│       ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│       └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
├── given oracle is fully configured — slippage enforcement
│   ├── when router output equals oracle floor exactly
│   │   └── it should succeed in execute
│   ├── when router output is above oracle floor
│   │   └── it should succeed in execute
│   └── when router output is below oracle floor
│       └── it should revert with DexSwapModule_InsufficientOutput
├── given oracle is fully configured — decimal normalization
│   ├── when sell and buy tokens have different decimals (6 and 18)
│   │   └── it should correctly normalize output
│   └── when price feeds have different decimals (8 and 18)
│       └── it should correctly normalize using feed decimals
├── given oracle is fully configured — estimateOutput
│   ├── it should return non-zero expected output
│   └── it should scale linearly
├── given oracle is fully configured — no residual state
│   └── it should hold no tokens after oracle rejection
└── fuzz
    ├── it should never revert on validate calls with arbitrary oracle data
    ├── it should enforce floor equals expected times slippage factor
    └── it should match mulDiv computation for estimateOutput
